<ns0:note style="-uslm-lc:I74" role="crossHeading" topic="editorialNotes" id="idb96ff42f-47c4-11f1-9a61-b1559996dfe8"><ns0:heading class="centered"><ns0:b>Editorial Notes</ns0:b></ns0:heading></ns0:note>
<ns0:note style="-uslm-lc:I74" topic="amendments" id="idb96ff430-47c4-11f1-9a61-b1559996dfe8"><ns0:heading class="centered smallCaps">Amendments</ns0:heading><ns0:p style="-uslm-lc:I21" class="indent0">2024—Subsec. (b)(1)(B). <ns0:ref href="/us/pl/118/159">Pub. L. 118–159</ns0:ref> inserted “or the Uniform Code of Military Justice” after “State law”.</ns0:p>
<ns0:p style="-uslm-lc:I21" class="indent0">2018—Subsec. (a). <ns0:ref href="/us/pl/115/392/s11/2/A">Pub. L. 115–392, § 11(2)(A)</ns0:ref>, substituted “3 times” for “twice”.</ns0:p>
<ns0:p style="-uslm-lc:I21" class="indent0">Subsec. (b)(1)(B). <ns0:ref href="/us/pl/115/392/s11/2/B">Pub. L. 115–392, § 11(2)(B)</ns0:ref>, substituted “subparagraph (A)” for “paragraph (1)”.</ns0:p>
<ns0:p style="-uslm-lc:I21" class="indent0">2008—Subsec. (b)(1)(A). <ns0:ref href="/us/pl/110/457">Pub. L. 110–457</ns0:ref> substituted “chapter 110, or section 1591” for “or chapter 110”.</ns0:p>
<ns0:p style="-uslm-lc:I21" class="indent0">2003—Subsec. (a). <ns0:ref href="/us/pl/108/21">Pub. L. 108–21</ns0:ref> inserted “, unless section 3559(e) applies” before period at end.</ns0:p>
</ns0:note>
